From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jon Pretty <jon.pretty@propensive.com>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:22:48 +0200
Subject: Box opaque-external type arguments in cast type applications

The type arguments of a type test or cast (e.g. the `asInstanceOf` an
opaque type's companion `apply` performs) skipped the argument-boxing
that every other spelling of an undealiasable type application receives
in `transformTT`/`normalizeCaptures`. The cast therefore minted an
unboxed spelling of a type whose canonical, declaration-side spelling
has boxed arguments, and the two failed to compare ('is boxed but ...
is not'), surfacing as inliner-proxy/aka-Tagged mismatches over
capturing singleton instances.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Proscala-Patch: castbox
---
 compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Setup.scala | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Setup.scala b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Setup.scala
index 162f8d80f628dda9ae7b2f8de6f2cd668108731a..d69a1aef92227ae48bc2c423c01225f67423c008 100644
--- a/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Setup.scala
+++ b/compiler/src/dotty/tools/dotc/cc/Setup.scala
@@ -684,8 +684,19 @@ class Setup extends PreRecheck, SymTransformer, SetupAPI:
             case _ => args.map(_ => NoType)
           for case (arg: TypeTree, formal) <- args.lazyZip(formals) do
             if defn.isTypeTestOrCast(fn.symbol) then
+              // Box the arguments of an undealiasable (e.g. opaque-external) type application
+              // in a cast's type argument, exactly as `normalizeCaptures` does for the same
+              // application elsewhere. Otherwise a cast — such as the one an opaque type's
+              // companion `apply` performs — produces an unboxed spelling of a type whose
+              // canonical (declaration-side) spelling has boxed arguments, and the two fail
+              // to compare ("is boxed but ... is not").
+              val boxedArgs = arg.tpe match
+                case tp @ AppliedType(tycon, args0)
+                if !defn.isFunctionClass(tp.dealias.typeSymbol) && (tp.dealias eq tp) =>
+                  tp.derivedAppliedType(tycon, args0.mapConserve(_.boxDeeply))
+                case tp => tp
               arg.setNuType(
-                globalCapToLocal(arg.tpe, Origin.TypeArg(arg.tpe)))
+                globalCapToLocal(boxedArgs, Origin.TypeArg(arg.tpe)))
               else
                 transformTT(arg, NoSymbol, boxed = true, typeArgFormal = formal) // type arguments in type applications are boxed
 
